.TH NETMAPPER 1 "2026-09-30" "netmapper 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
netmapper \- concurrent TCP and UDP scanner for authorized network inventory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B netmapper
.B \-t
.I target
[B\-tR ItargetR ...]
[B\-pR IportsR | B\-\-top-portsR InR]
[B\-cR InR]
[B\-\-timeout-msR ImillisecondsR]
[B\-\-formatR Itable|jsonR]
[B\-oR IfileR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B netmapper
resolves IPv4 and IPv6 addresses, CIDR networks, and DNS names, then probes selected TCP and/or UDP ports. TCP uses connect probes. UDP sends DNS and NTP requests on their conventional ports and an empty datagram elsewhere. UDP silence is reported as open|filtered because it cannot distinguish a silent service from packet loss. The scanner uses bounded concurrency and enforces limits of 4,096 resolved addresses and 1,000,000 probes per run.
.PP
Only scan systems and networks that you own or are explicitly authorized to assess.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-t , \ \-\-target \ target
Target IP address, CIDR network, or DNS name. Repeat this option for multiple targets.
.TP
.BR \-p , \ \-\-ports \ ports
Comma-separated ports and inclusive ranges, for example 22,53,80,443,8000-8100. Port zero is invalid. Defaults to the built-in 100-port common set.
.TP
.BR \-\-top-ports \ n
Use the first 1 to 100 entries from the built-in common-port set. The set is not claimed to match Nmap's port ranking.
.TP
.BR \-c , \ \-\-concurrency \ n
Maximum simultaneous probes per protocol, from 1 to 8192. Default: 512.
.TP
.BR \ \-\-scan-mode \ mode
Select tcp (default), udp, or both.
.TP
.BR \-s , \ \-\-service-detection
Collect banners from open TCP ports. HTTP ports receive a HEAD request; other ports are read for a passive banner. This is not exhaustive Nmap service fingerprinting.
.TP
.BR \-\-timeout-ms \ milliseconds
Per-probe timeout, from 50 to 60000 milliseconds. Default: 1000.
.TP
.BR \ \-\-format \ format
Output as BtableR (default) or BjsonR.
.TP
.BR \-o , \ \-\-output \ file
Write formatted results to a file instead of standard output.
.TP
.BR \-h , \ \-\-help
Print command help.
.TP
.BR \-V , \ \-\-version
Print version.
.SH STATES
.TP
.B open
The TCP connection completed or a UDP response was received.
.TP
.B closed
The remote endpoint explicitly refused the TCP connection.
.TP
.B filtered
The attempt timed out or failed without an explicit connection refusal. This is an inference and does not prove a firewall caused the result.
.TP
.B open|filtered
A UDP probe received no response before timeout. The port may be open or filtered.
.SH LIMITATIONS
This version does not implement raw SYN/ACK scans, OS fingerprinting, TLS service fingerprints, traceroute, Nmap scripts, or Nmap XML output. The service column is a static port-number hint. Banner collection is limited to HTTP response headers and passive TCP banners; it is not full Nmap service/version detection. Scanning can trigger monitoring alerts and network policy controls.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Scan a host using the built-in common ports:
.B netmapper -t 192.0.2.15
.TP
Scan selected ports on an authorized target:
.B netmapper -t app.example.test -p 22,80,443,8000-8100
.TP
Write JSON results to a file:
.B netmapper -t 192.0.2.15 -p 22,443 --format json -o scan.json
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nmap (1)